From 9007000000000000000000000000000000000007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MinsOS <minsos@localhost>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Enable AppLock CoreRune (One UI 8.5)

In stock firmware, CoreRune.FW_SUPPORT_APPLOCK and CoreRune.FW_APPLOCK are
only enabled if SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_SMARTMANAGER_CONFIG_PACKAGE_NAME equals
"com.samsung.android.sm_cn" (China Smart Manager).

Setting CoreRune.FW_SUPPORT_APPLOCK = true and CoreRune.FW_APPLOCK = true
opens the framework gates in AppLockPolicy, ActivityStarter, and
ActivityTaskManagerService so that application locking is supported by the OS.

---
diff --git a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune.smali
@@ -3511,9 +3511,7 @@
 
     const-string v9, "com.samsung.android.sm_cn"
 
-    invoke-virtual {v2, v9}, Ljava/lang/String;->equals(Ljava/lang/Object;)Z
-
-    move-result v2
+    const/4 v2, 0x1
 
     sput-boolean v2, Lcom/samsung/android/rune/CoreRune;->FW_SUPPORT_APPLOCK:Z
 
-- 
2.51.0
